    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first Rescue Bridge, built around 1913, linked the village to Battery Park and made mail delivery easier for residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rescue%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Two historic churches sit just outside the Village Center: Riverview United Methodist (1887) and Friends Church (1913).",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rescue%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Rescue’s Village Center includes homes, two marinas, a restaurant, a post office, and a former school turned community hall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rescue%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The village lies on Jones Creek, about half a mile from its mouth where it meets the James River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
